TASK-169 runtime harness: a hover-revealed sidebar that must hide again.
Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task169-harness.patch
    xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    OUT="$PWD/.derived-logs/task169"; mkdir -p "$OUT"
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify169 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # wait for the "done" line in $OUT/verify.log (about 40 s), then kill that pid
    git apply -R docs/harness/task169-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

What it does: puts the window in auto-hide mode, moves the window (never the
pointer) so that the sidebar is away from the real pointer, and reports the
edge enter and sidebar exit that tracking areas would send, by calling
sidebarHoverZoneEntered / sidebarHoverZoneExited. Real tracking-area events
are not produced: posted mouse-moved events do not generate them. S1 and S2
use the real pointer position; S3 to S6 replace it through
sidebarPointerProbeForTesting.

    S1  exit inside the reveal grace period      hides about 1 s after the reveal
    S2  no exit at all                           hides about 1.25 s after the reveal
    S3  pointer inside, then outside, no exit    stays, then hides
    S4  popover shown, pointer leaves            stays until the popover closes
    S5  Toggle Sidebar while revealed            pinned, stays
    S6  context menu open, pointer outside       stays while the menu is open

S7 runs only with DETOUR_VERIFY_UNDER_POINTER set: it moves the window under
the real pointer and away again, to check "stays while the real pointer is
over it" without a stand-in. It puts a window under the pointer of whoever is
at the machine and tells nothing if they move the pointer meanwhile.

